(Infrastructure) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Decision) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Syrka should use a hybrid approach with Open edX as the primary open-source LMS foundation, ) Tj
T*
(not a direct long-lived fork of a traditional LMS.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The recommended foundation is:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Adopt Open edX concepts, data/event patterns, XBlock/LTI compatibility, course-authoring ) Tj
T*
(semantics, assessment primitives, and selected service boundaries as the Syrka LMS skeleton.) Tj
T*
(2. Do not make the Open edX monolith the permanent Syrka product core. Instead, wrap it ) Tj
T*
(during phase 1 and progressively extract domain capabilities into Syrka-native services on ) Tj
T*
(the existing Next.js/Supabase stack.) Tj
T*
(3. Use LTI 1.3 / Advantage as the integration contract for external tools, assignments, ) Tj
T*
(simulations, code workspaces, AI tutors, and assessment engines.) Tj
T*
(4. Treat the LMS as a capability-data collection engine whose primary product responsibility) Tj
T*
( is to produce normalized learning, evidence, credential, and collaboration events for the ) Tj
T*
(Syrka Ontology, Human Capability Graph, Capability Inference Engine, Career Intent Engine, ) Tj
T*
(Odyssey, Job Passport, and Workforce Mobility Engine.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This is not a recommendation to become "an Open edX company." It is a recommendation to use ) Tj
T*
(Open edX as the strongest available open-source educational operating substrate while ) Tj
T*
(protecting Syrka's long-term architecture with an anti-corruption layer, canonical event ) Tj
T*
(schema, independent ontology/graph services, and Syrka-native user experiences.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
