T*
(12. Why alternatives were rejected) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Build completely from scratch) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Rejected because Syrka would spend years rebuilding commodity LMS operations: enrolments, ) Tj
T*
(assignments, quizzes, gradebooks, content handling, course authoring, roles, permissions, ) Tj
T*
(and LTI. The strategic value is not a blank LMS; it is capability inference and workforce ) Tj
T*
(mobility. Scratch-building the operational LMS delays the actual company-defining platform.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Fork Moodle) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Rejected as primary direction because Moodle's strengths are plugin breadth and ) Tj
T*
(institutional maturity, not AI-native architecture. It is viable as an operational LMS, but ) Tj
T*
(a long-lived Syrka fork would inherit a large PHP monolith and modernization drag.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Fork Canvas LMS) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Rejected as primary direction despite strong APIs and PostgreSQL alignment because it is a ) Tj
T*
(large Rails product shaped by Instructure's SaaS priorities, has AGPL obligations, and is ) Tj
T*
(less naturally aligned with modular learning component authoring and Python AI pipelines ) Tj
T*
(than Open edX.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Fork Open edX directly) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Rejected as stated because a permanent direct fork risks trapping Syrka inside a heavy ) Tj
T*
(monolith. The accepted decision is Open edX hybrid: adopt, wrap, instrument, and extract.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Fork Chamilo) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Rejected because it is too lightweight for Syrka's long-term capability infrastructure and ) Tj
T*
(event/AI ambitions.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Fork ILIAS) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Rejected because it is mature but specialized, PHP-heavy, and less compatible with the ) Tj
T*
(modern AI-native, graph-driven, Vercel/Next.js/Supabase-oriented Syrka direction.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Fork Sakai) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Rejected because its license and service orientation are attractive, but the Java/Tomcat ) Tj
T*
(architecture and older frontend model are not the best fit for rapid AI-native product ) Tj
ET
endstream
